(ARCHITECTURE AND FEATURE SEMANTICS) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Process layout:) Tj T*
(  Erlang escript controller \(OTP peer lifecycle and measurements\)) Tj T*
(    -> Engine OS process: application -> supervisor -> reddit_server) Tj T*
(    -> Client OS process 0: coordinator -> one process per assigned user) Tj T*
(    -> Client OS process 1: coordinator -> one process per assigned user) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Engine calls cross node boundaries using distributed Erlang gen_server calls.) Tj T*
(Each client node owns its metrics collector. One-second resource samplers run) Tj T*
(on the engine and both client nodes. The controller stops peers in cleanup.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(reddit_engine contains pure state transitions. The gen_server serializes) Tj T*
(updates atomically; maps index accounts, communities, content, memberships,) Tj T*
(votes, comments, child comments, inboxes and per-community post IDs.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Creating a community joins its creator. Joining/leaving is idempotent.) Tj T*
(Posting and commenting require membership. Posts contain plain text only.) Tj T*
(Comments reference a post plus an optional parent comment; a parent from) Tj T*
(another post is rejected. Arbitrary depth is represented without recursion) Tj T*
(in storage, and thread reads expose parent IDs for reconstruction.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Each user has one vote per post/comment, with values -1, 0, +1. Replacing or) Tj T*
(removing a vote applies its delta to content score and the author's karma.) Tj T*
(Self-voting is rejected; new content starts at zero score.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Feeds merge posts from joined communities, newest ID first, with exclusive) Tj T*
(ID cursors and limits of 1-100. Content IDs provide stable ordering.) Tj T*
(Reposts retain the source post ID while receiving their own IDs and votes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Inboxes expose only messages addressed to the caller. Only recipients can) Tj T*
(reply; replies reference the previous message. Offline recipients retain) Tj T*
(messages, memberships and content, and recover access on reconnect.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Responses are {ok,Value} or {error,Reason}; reasons include duplicate,) Tj T*
(invalid, not_found, forbidden, offline, timeout and unavailable. OTP call) Tj T*
(references correlate requests. Mutation timeouts are never auto-retried.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The supervisor restarts a crashed engine with empty state. The benchmark) Tj T*
(checks the engine PID and rejects a run if the server restarted.) Tj T*
ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 270 30 Td (2 / 7) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
