(SIMULATOR AND MEASUREMENT METHOD) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Users are partitioned by user ID modulo the number of client nodes.) Tj T*
(Every user is a real Erlang process with seeded PRNG state. Setup registers) Tj T*
(users, joins communities, and seeds posts, comments and direct-message threads.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The target member count at subreddit rank r is max\(1, floor\(N/r^1.1\)\).) Tj T*
(A rank-specific cyclic permutation selects exactly that many distinct users.) Tj T*
(Each subreddit also contains one seed account. Rank 1 contains every user.) Tj T*
(The benchmark checks all 100 observed membership counts against the targets.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Online users wait a random initial phase, choose an action, await its reply,) Tj T*
(and sleep 1000 ms. Default action probabilities are 30% feed, 25% post,) Tj T*
(20% comment, 15% vote, 5% messaging and 5% membership changes. A membership) Tj T*
(action issues leave plus join. Lifecycle requests are measured separately.) Tj T*
(10% of posting actions are reposts. Half of comment actions target a prior) Tj T*
(comment; cached per-community parents allow comment depth to grow.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Users stay online for 5-15 seconds, then offline for 2-5 seconds. Offline) Tj T*
(users issue no activity requests. These are application-level disconnections:) Tj T*
(client worker nodes remain alive to simulate many independent users.) Tj T*
(Choosing among joined subreddits makes popular communities receive more) Tj T*
(posting traffic. The results include member/post-count correlation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Each run starts with a fresh engine. Setup is excluded, followed by 10 seconds) Tj T*
(of warmup and 30 seconds of measurement. Seeds 42/43/44 are used for three) Tj T*
(repetitions at 100, 1000 and 10000 users. Larger probes use seed 42.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Offered requests are counted by start time; completions by response time.) Tj T*
(Window-boundary in-flight calls may make the totals differ. Latencies use) Tj T*
(bounded power-of-two millisecond histograms; reported percentiles are upper) Tj T*
(bounds, not exact samples. A 1 ms bucket includes sub-millisecond replies.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The success criterion is >=99% successful observed completions, <1% timeouts,) Tj T*
(p95 <1000 ms, and no sustained mailbox growth. Growth means six consecutive) Tj T*
(increasing samples ending above 100 queued requests. It is a heuristic.) Tj T*
(Larger probes stop after a failed run/criterion or the sweep time budget.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This is a closed-loop simulation: latency and offline periods reduce offered) Tj T*
(load. User population is reported separately from active request throughput.) Tj T*
ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 270 30 Td (3 / 7) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
